9IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation progress: added only the signed-plan file impact, .codex/config.toml. Pinned Serena at c7dbe3bd1198cf451bf7aa8fdeeab88571fa3a6e, context=codex, --project-from-cwd, startup_timeout_sec=120, enabled=true, required unset. Validation: tomllib structural/value assertions passed; codex mcp list in the worktree shows enabled serena with exact pinned argv; a 120-second-bounded Python MCP SDK client completed initialize + tools/list in 4.3s, auto-detected /Users/joeoakhart/config-c622-serena, exposed 24 tools, and included find_symbol/find_referencing_symbols/get_symbols_overview/replace_symbol_body/insert_after_symbol; /tmp negative control showed no project-scoped serena. make lint and make typecheck pass; full default test gate is running. Review advisory to update AGENTS.md was deferred to preserve the ticket's signed single-file scope: the existing clause is explicitly a Claude diagnostic, while the Codex configuration itself is self-discoverable via codex mcp list and the ticket records that recovery command.","timestamp":1785620891494655001}],"created_at":1785619173860806001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1dd63f36-a475-421f-8f02-ebf1e0f2686f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9109-2ad9-2477-4cf6"}],"description":"## Context\nCodex currently has no Serena MCP entry, while this project relies on Serena/Pyright for semantic navigation. The tracked `.claude/settings.json` does not configure MCP servers. Separately, this operator machine's untracked Claude project config (`~/.claude.json`) launches Serena via `uvx --from git+https://github.com/oraios/serena`; that machine-local fact was inspected only to identify the existing server. The delivery design is independently grounded: the current Codex manual supports project-scoped MCP servers in trusted `.codex/config.toml`, and Serena 1.6.2.dev0 exposes a `codex` context plus `--project-from-cwd` specifically for CLI agents/worktrees.\n\n## Verified inputs\n- `uvx --from git+https://github.com/oraios/serena serena -V` returned `Serena 1.6.2.dev0`.\n- `git ls-remote https://github.com/oraios/serena.git HEAD` returned `c7dbe3bd1198cf451bf7aa8fdeeab88571fa3a6e`.\n- `uvx --from git+https://github.com/oraios/serena@c7dbe3bd1198cf451bf7aa8fdeeab88571fa3a6e serena start-mcp-server --help` succeeded and documented `--context` plus `--project-from-cwd`.\n- `codex mcp list` in the current worktree confirms no `serena` entry exists before the change.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a project-scoped `mcp_servers.serena` STDIO entry to `.codex/config.toml`; project scope is intentional so every contributor/worktree gets the repo-required semantic navigation server after trusting the repo, without mutating each operator's global config.\n- Launch the same Serena distribution currently used on this machine, but pin the verified upstream commit: `uvx --from git+https://github.com/oraios/serena@c7dbe3bd1198cf451bf7aa8fdeeab88571fa3a6e`.\n- Pass `serena start-mcp-server --context codex --project-from-cwd` so each checkout/worktree activates itself; commit no user-specific project path.\n- Set `startup_timeout_sec = 120` to bound and accommodate a cold uvx resolution. Keep `required` unset/false so a Serena startup failure is reported by Codex without preventing all Codex work.\n- Validate TOML with Python 3.11+ `tomllib`; run `codex mcp list` from the isolated worktree and require an enabled `serena` row containing the pinned command/args; run the pinned `serena start-mcp-server --help` command and an MCP initialize/list-tools smoke test from the worktree, bounded by a test harness timeout.\n- Negative control: run `codex mcp list` from a temporary untrusted/non-rebar directory and confirm the project-scoped server is not injected there.\n- Land the single-file config change through Gerrit with DCO and the ticket trailer.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `codex mcp list` from a trusted rebar worktree discovers an enabled `serena` STDIO server from `.codex/config.toml`, using the pinned upstream commit.\n- [ ] The server argv uses Serena's `codex` context and `--project-from-cwd`; no user-specific rebar path is committed.\n- [ ] `python -c \"import tomllib; tomllib.load(open('.codex/config.toml', 'rb'))\"`, the pinned Serena CLI smoke command, and an MCP initialize/list-tools smoke test all succeed.\n- [ ] `codex mcp list` outside the trusted rebar project does not expose the project-scoped `serena` entry; Serena startup remains non-required so failure does not block Codex itself.\n- [ ] The config diff contains no secrets, and `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the default suite remain green; a same-base full-gate result may be reused because this task changes only static Codex configuration.\n\n## References\nCurrent Codex manual: trusted projects may scope MCP servers in `.codex/config.toml`; STDIO entries accept `command`, `args`, `cwd`, `startup_timeout_sec`, and optional `required`. Serena CLI help at the pinned commit documents `--context codex` and `--project-from-cwd`.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":".codex/config.toml","reason":"project-scoped Serena STDIO MCP registration for Codex"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","9109-2ad9-2477-4cf6"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"b514cfa6-abf0-423d-8fcd-8dc4f46b0cff","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["codex","serena","mcp"],"ticket_id":"c622-8877-f677-4535","ticket_type":"task","title":"Configure Codex to use the project's Serena MCP server","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["39fdcfe6-a695-426f-81ad-092a8b95ee0d","e1e879b7-11b6-4ad2-8723-eeae5d15f18f","1dd63f36-a475-421f-8f02-ebf1e0f2686f","852668f6-6db2-4c53-a4b3-7b6492646a53","679156d2-deeb-48c5-9279-04549e595bf1","b514cfa6-abf0-423d-8fcd-8dc4f46b0cff","9d66cea5-b664-49d4-9409-c7900c9d1dc2","ef42f3ec-5d42-4683-9f74-6e9a46aca8dc"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785620891494655002,"uuid":"e7b7dcd1-ad09-495d-83d6-565e63d9266d"}